            },
            {
                "entry_id": "c225381a-3631-3451-bbda-3e972b0b1f9d",
                "word": "médiocrate",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "d323445e-7ac1-4587-86e8-43e478373645",
                        "entry_id": "c225381a-3631-3451-bbda-3e972b0b1f9d",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "médiocrates"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "069cfd24-4e14-3768-ba55-8dc8f694a398",
                        "entry_id": "c225381a-3631-3451-bbda-3e972b0b1f9d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Dirigeant médiocre ; membre d’une médiocratie."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "pejorative",
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ed70de5-ae9b-4391-9289-73c81ad94090",
                                "sense_id": "069cfd24-4e14-3768-ba55-8dc8f694a398",
                                "text": "Les manies chez les médiocrates sont souvent deux à deux."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c6fc9bb4-45a0-4fd9-9f54-3e795fa74045",
                                "sense_id": "069cfd24-4e14-3768-ba55-8dc8f694a398",
                                "text": "Qui est-ce qui pourrait vouloir être meilleur que les autres, et avoir une autre probité que celle de « tout le monde » ? Pourquoi ne ferait-on pas d’affaires ? Pourquoi ne toucherait-on pas une petite commission ? […] C’est la « médiocratie » morale, et le député qui sait à l’occasion, sans bruit, et en douceur, « faire rendre » à ses votes, loin d’indigner l’honnête et brave électeur, lui inspire plutôt une tendresse, la tendresse d’un médiocrate pour un autre médiocrate. Comment ! on serait des filous, des voleurs, des bandits, parce qu’on aurait touché des chèques ? Pas du tout ! On est « comme tout le monde », des « médiocrates », de simples médiocrates !"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ae94372-7c3b-48ab-9bbc-dbd67b873606",
                                "sense_id": "069cfd24-4e14-3768-ba55-8dc8f694a398",
                                "text": "Or, ce monsieur du pouvoir exécutif, et ces médiocrates de province, ont le chauvinisme de la tragédie, du personnage noble."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b30844bb-d33c-433c-9938-3916c72a20de",
                                "sense_id": "069cfd24-4e14-3768-ba55-8dc8f694a398",
                                "text": "Sachons déjouer les manœuvres de ceux qui, se prétendant artistocrates, agissent dans toutes les circonstances de leur vie en médiocrates."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "af07a6da-f70b-4bf4-8fea-bf4f4d066e4c",
                        "source_entry_id": "c225381a-3631-3451-bbda-3e972b0b1f9d",
                        "source_sense_id": "069cfd24-4e14-3768-ba55-8dc8f694a398",
                        "target_lang_word": "mediocrat",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mediocrat",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8da6f62a-d79c-36a5-b331-08d5b6632503",
                                        "entry_id": "3428c8e0-f0d8-36ac-b54b-7d51dd81eb94",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A politician or bureaucrat of mediocre ability."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5cd29a7-c5a4-4a3b-abc9-e3a0cdf86237",
                                                "sense_id": "8da6f62a-d79c-36a5-b331-08d5b6632503",
                                                "text": "The Oligarchs — remnants from Brazil's colonial past — are sub-divided into the well-intentioned but provincial \"mediocrats\" and the more highly powered \"kleptocrats\" — thieves of the first order."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bc8376e6-6c9b-4f83-bcbe-32e8f2b920ca",
                                                "sense_id": "8da6f62a-d79c-36a5-b331-08d5b6632503",
                                                "text": "In India, men and women of talent, ability, honesty and integrity keep their distance from the politics of today. It is a game of mediocrats."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9022c124-b2bd-4e05-8f19-d89fccac1e03",
                                                "sense_id": "8da6f62a-d79c-36a5-b331-08d5b6632503",
                                                "text": "It was argued by Jayashree (1999) and by Sadri and Jayashree (2002) that the greatest hindrance to organisational progress is the mediocrat - the bureaucrat who tries to guard his turf since he is inherently insecure."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "76a1de5d-1569-3b08-b796-e5f386a7cb27",
                                        "entry_id": "3428c8e0-f0d8-36ac-b54b-7d51dd81eb94",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An advocate of mediocracy; one who prefers to avoid controversy, change and risk."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "675c956f-028a-4acb-a9ec-26b253226c3e",
                                                "sense_id": "76a1de5d-1569-3b08-b796-e5f386a7cb27",
                                                "text": "There is in Canadian political, business, and social life a certain formality and conservatism that reflect this fact. This conservatism has its regrettable side, of course. The walking dead are out in numbers - the mediocrats, the anti-hothead vote."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "850d2e49-24f2-426e-a829-34c7d7e87299",
                                                "sense_id": "76a1de5d-1569-3b08-b796-e5f386a7cb27",
                                                "text": "Perhaps this Utopia of the mediocrats is not so far off; perhaps it is time for the meritocracy to assert itself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6da4bb38-b311-43f1-9731-6fa254a8dc8d",
                                                "sense_id": "76a1de5d-1569-3b08-b796-e5f386a7cb27",
                                                "text": "And our mediocrats are satisfied. Mediocrity is not, of course, a specifically modern sin; what is specifically modern is its overwhelming acceptance as the normal condition of humanity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7e3f9bd-adfe-4b07-979b-c1dd4f8362cf",
                                                "sense_id": "76a1de5d-1569-3b08-b796-e5f386a7cb27",
                                                "text": "First of all, we have to scrap the mediocrats' approach. We have to reward excellence without going to a superstar mentality, and we have to take care that at all times all the possibilities are covered."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d57b67ad-69d6-30b1-a1a1-47edb97f53f3",
                                        "entry_id": "3428c8e0-f0d8-36ac-b54b-7d51dd81eb94",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An ordinary person with no special abilities; a mediocrity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af6d2f68-61bc-4c80-b533-e4ad7adfaf71",
                                                "sense_id": "d57b67ad-69d6-30b1-a1a1-47edb97f53f3",
                                                "text": "Follow the big top, even if you're only one of the crowd, only a mediocrat, as Vesta says."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2674c11-00ac-46bf-aa88-8f189e5ca537",
                                                "sense_id": "d57b67ad-69d6-30b1-a1a1-47edb97f53f3",
                                                "text": "Not only is marriage a prerequisite for these groups, but in all other respects the joiners sound like archetypical mediocrats. Their average income is about $10,000 a year; the most heavily represented occupational categories are “salesman” and \"housewife,\" and the average age is thirty to fifty."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1bf6dc40-c967-4da7-999d-ba4504c5e686",
                                                "sense_id": "d57b67ad-69d6-30b1-a1a1-47edb97f53f3",
                                                "text": "The world evolution is out of mediocrats. You cannot expect all to be Nobel Prize winners or scientists of the rank of Newton."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c73de67d-1dcd-3848-b9ae-ce576c9ca745",
                                        "entry_id": "3428c8e0-f0d8-36ac-b54b-7d51dd81eb94",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A politician or leader from a middle-class background."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55c1a5cf-1033-47cf-9539-1dff9d75e266",
                                                "sense_id": "c73de67d-1dcd-3848-b9ae-ce576c9ca745",
                                                "text": "A Council like this, constituted as it will be exclusively of the ruling chiefs and territorial magnates, will be a mere ornamental body, hardly competent to give sound advice to Government in all important matters. In India it is the mediocrat who have received the light of education, and it is they whou can render good advice for the solution of the important political problems that may arise in the administration of this country."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f1e2d93-8fa6-4fe4-a5e6-582677717322",
                                                "sense_id": "c73de67d-1dcd-3848-b9ae-ce576c9ca745",
                                                "text": "Increasingly, it is through these media-anointed mediocrats — Reverend Al Sharpton for New York's black dispossessed microculture, to cite one example — that microcultures talk to one another."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "529e474a-697c-3c71-a340-27ccc05938a0",
                                        "entry_id": "3428c8e0-f0d8-36ac-b54b-7d51dd81eb94",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A plant species that thrives in moderate conditions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "509a5493-64c1-44f8-a96e-2dc4dc231f09",
                                                "sense_id": "529e474a-697c-3c71-a340-27ccc05938a0",
                                                "text": "In our opinion it is impossible to consider Taxodiaceae as a characteristic index of a warm climate and therefore they cannot be included in the typical mediocrats group,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "732e4f36-73ba-4b31-85d0-f8dadbf4c2ac",
                                                "sense_id": "529e474a-697c-3c71-a340-27ccc05938a0",
                                                "text": "The sharp increase in terminocrats and the decrease in mediocrats between marker beds f and h should correspond to renewed cooling."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "030478c3-7ad8-4b88-9269-0191d3f20176",
                                                "sense_id": "529e474a-697c-3c71-a340-27ccc05938a0",
                                                "text": "The mediocrats (see “mesocratic” in Figure 15.8) curve refers to Quercus, Tilia, Ulmus, and other trees/shrubs characteristic of the climatic-optimum part of interglacials."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
